<title>BRAZIL: RESEARCH ALERT-Petrobras maintained.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Petrobras maintained.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morgan Stanley Dean Witter said it was maintaining its outperform rating on Brazilian state oil firm Petrobras and raising its 12-month price target to $340 per 1,000 shares.</p>
<p>-- Analysts Lloyd Byrne and Hillary Peruzzi said in a report the stock could face near-term volatility, providing the opportunity for attractive entry points over the coming months.</p>
<p>-- said the stock is partially discounting several positive scenarios, including the Brazilian Congress moving forward with the oil deregulation bill, an increase in international capital flowing to the company and a positive macroeconomic climate.</p>
<p>-- Petrobras preferred was up 0.66 percent at 306 reais in midafternoon trade on the Sao Paulo bolsa.</p>
<p>((--Fatima Cristina, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485412))</p>
